  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    An orca raider of middling rank during the Orca Incursion, practitioner of the Gut Inversion technique and the Grend Blood-Arts, and instigator of the Shelf Crushing Offense — the forty-three-day siege against the volcanic vents of Nightfall Shelf, the tunnel-dwelling penguin colony.
    
    Zund Gnasharkin trained under Thung Thrakrek, a war-leader whose teachings he absorbed without apparent ambition for independent authority. His left fin was ritually split in the blood-speaker manner, though he never claimed shamanic rank. He carried Grungruk's Claw, a pressure-forged trident of blackened whale-bone that sang when it tasted blood, for eight seasons — a duration I accept provisionally, as orca seasonal reckoning is imprecise by penguin standards.
    
    His jaw bore scar tissue from a counter-strike by ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer, a Nightshelf tunnel-fighter who would outlive him. He refused healing. He guarded the maimed flank of his pod-brother Grul Grulrend without being asked, and he insisted on accounting for every kill — carving a distinctive mark into ice, a practice precise enough that the signatures remained identifiable long after his death.
    
    The chronicle *Interrogation Record: Threk-Bone-Day Incident* places Zund among those who reviewed pod-authority documents following a war-ritual after which Grungruk's Claw reportedly sang without feeding. He noted this change with unease. I note that the interrogation record survives while whatever unease he recorded does not.
    
    Zund marshaled three war-pods against Nightfall Shelf's fire-barriers. The siege ended when merchant-guild sorcerers of Weal' Clique collapsed the upper galleries rather than permit breach of the colony's deepest fire-veins. Zund died pinned beneath the ice, still driving his weapon into the shelf. Grungruk's Claw went dark. Its subsequent corruption and Grul Grulrend's retrieval of it are addressed in those entries.
