  annotation "note_1771588268468_0", anchor: "merchant-guild sorcerers of Weal' Clique collapsed the upper galleries rather than permit breach", text: "I have erased Aureate. The cross-reference names both Weal' Clique~ and Aureate casting Pod-bond Annihilation in mutual sacrifice — two individuals choosing to die together to bring a shelf down on an army. I reduced this to 'merchant-guild sorcerers' performing a tactical demolition, as though they were collapsing a mine rather than themselves. Aureate's entry addresses what she was. This sentence should have named her. Compression is not an excuse for erasure, and I know better.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771588268468_1", anchor: "carving a distinctive mark into ice, a practice precise enough that the signatures remained identifiable long after his death", text: "An orca raider keeping meticulous kill-records frozen into the medium I have spent my career reading. He was building an archive. He did not call it that — he would have called it honor, or debt, or the weight a predator owes what it takes. But the marks survived. They are legible. Someone carved accountability into ice and it outlasted him, his pod-brother, the shelf he broke himself against. How extraordinary that an orca understood what ice is for before most penguins did.", type: :commentary, display: :full
